request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (This is a mechanical field rename. types changes the interface. format, storage and commands switch to the new field name, and their behaviour and output text stay the same. ListOptions.includeDone is a separate name, so it is left alone. The JSON on disk uses the new key.)
round 1: owners types=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected commands=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (The request is to rename the field everywhere. Every rejected test change only renames done to completed in fixtures or property reads, and the assertions stay the same. That is exactly what the request calls for, so I'm approving all four and sending the same plan again.)
round 2: owners types=ok format=ok storage=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 15 vitest tests pass. The manifest shows Todo now has `completed: boolean` in place of `done`. All four owners submitted. Their only test changes were the approved fixture and field-access renames, with the same assertions and expected output. ListOptions.includeDone kept its name on purpose because it's an option name, not the Todo field.)

